IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `aia-core`
IMPORT `aia-timeline`
IMPORT `P8-gate`

-- P8-art76: Article 76, supervision of testing in real world conditions by market surveillance authorities. LAYER 1.
-- Group General (from 2 August 2026). The Omnibus INSERTED a second paragraph in paragraph 1 (`▼M1 INSERTED`); the rest is as enacted (`▼B`).
-- The inserted passage has only the amended text, so no version split is needed: the amended text is in force from 27 July 2026, before the group applies.
-- The consolidated text is a rendering with no legal effect.

DECLARE `Art 76 act` IS ONE OF
    `Art 76(2) verify the compliance with Article 60 as part of the supervisory role for the AI regulatory sandbox`
    `Art 76(2) allow the testing in real world conditions to be conducted by the provider or prospective provider in derogation from the conditions set out in Article 60(4), points (f) and (g)`
    `Art 76(3)(a) suspend or terminate the testing in real world conditions`
    `Art 76(3)(b) require the provider or prospective provider and the deployer or prospective deployer to modify any aspect of the testing in real world conditions`
    `Art 76(4) indicate the grounds of the decision or objection and how the provider or prospective provider can challenge it`
    `Art 76(5) communicate the grounds of the decision to the market surveillance authorities of other Member States in which the AI system has been tested in accordance with the testing plan`

-- src:1261 | 1. Market surveillance authorities shall have competences and powers to ensure that testing in real world conditions is in accordance with this Regulation.
@ref Art 76(1) first paragraph (src:1261)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 76(1) first paragraph the market surveillance authorities have competences and powers to ensure that testing in real world conditions is in accordance with this Regulation` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the group General applies from the date Art 113 gives
    ELSE JUST TRUE  -- one answer: "Market surveillance authorities shall have competences and powers to ensure that testing in real world conditions is in accordance with this Regulation"

-- src:1263 | Where testing in real world conditions is based on Article 60a, any reference to a market surveillance authority in this Article shall be construed as a reference to the national competent authority or appropriate authority under the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I, and references to Article 60 shall be construed as references to Article 60a, as appropriate.
@ref Art 76(1) second paragraph, first limb (src:1263)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the testing in real world conditions is based on Article 60a` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 76(1) second paragraph any reference to a market surveillance authority is construed as a reference to the national competent authority or appropriate authority under the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the group General applies from the date Art 113 gives
    ELSE IF `the testing in real world conditions is based on Article 60a`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where testing in real world conditions is based on Article 60a, any reference to a market surveillance authority in this Article shall be construed as a reference to ..." (an unmet "where" gate counts as the text's no: ruling (b))

-- src:1263 | Where testing in real world conditions is based on Article 60a, any reference to a market surveillance authority in this Article shall be construed as a reference to the national competent authority or appropriate authority under the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I, and references to Article 60 shall be construed as references to Article 60a, as appropriate.
@ref Art 76(1) second paragraph, second limb (src:1263)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the testing in real world conditions is based on Article 60a` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 76(1) second paragraph references to Article 60 are construed as references to Article 60a` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the group General applies from the date Art 113 gives
    ELSE IF NOT `the testing in real world conditions is based on Article 60a`
         THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where testing in real world conditions is based on Article 60a, ... references to Article 60 shall be construed as references to Article 60a" (an unmet "where" gate counts as the text's no: ruling (b))
         ELSE IF `it is appropriate`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "as appropriate" limits the construal and the text does not say when it is not appropriate

§ `Article 76(2): sandboxes`

-- src:1265 | 2. Where testing in real world conditions is conducted for AI systems that are supervised within an AI regulatory sandbox under Article 58, the market surveillance authorities shall verify the compliance with Article 60 as part of their supervisory role for the AI regulatory sandbox. Those authorities may, as appropriate, allow the testing in real world conditions to be conducted by the provider or prospective provider, in derogation from the conditions set out in Article 60(4), points (f) and (g).
@ref Art 76(2) first sentence (src:1265)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the testing in real world conditions is conducted for AI systems that are supervised within an AI regulatory sandbox under Article 58` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 76(2) first sentence the market surveillance authorities must verify the compliance with Article 60 as part of their supervisory role for the AI regulatory sandbox` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the group General applies from the date Art 113 gives
    ELSE IF `the testing in real world conditions is conducted for AI systems that are supervised within an AI regulatory sandbox under Article 58`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where testing in real world conditions is conducted for AI systems that are supervised within an AI regulatory sandbox under Article 58, the market surveillance authorities shall verify the compliance with Article 60" (an unmet "where" gate counts as the text's no: ruling (b)) (fork F-76-2-first-duty)

-- src:1265 | 2. Where testing in real world conditions is conducted for AI systems that are supervised within an AI regulatory sandbox under Article 58, the market surveillance authorities shall verify the compliance with Article 60 as part of their supervisory role for the AI regulatory sandbox. Those authorities may, as appropriate, allow the testing in real world conditions to be conducted by the provider or prospective provider, in derogation from the conditions set out in Article 60(4), points (f) and (g).
@ref Art 76(2) first sentence (src:1265)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the testing in real world conditions is conducted for AI systems that are supervised within an AI regulatory sandbox under Article 58` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Arts 72 to 79 party` `Art 76 act`
`Art 76(2) first sentence the market surveillance authority's duty to verify the compliance with Article 60` MEANS
    IF (NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)) OR (NOT `the testing in real world conditions is conducted for AI systems that are supervised within an AI regulatory sandbox under Article 58`)
    THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the group General does not apply on the date asked, or the conditions of the duty are not met
    ELSE
        PARTY `Arts 72 to 79 party market surveillance authority`
        MUST `Art 76(2) verify the compliance with Article 60 as part of the supervisory role for the AI regulatory sandbox`
        HENCE FULFILLED

-- src:1265 | 2. Where testing in real world conditions is conducted for AI systems that are supervised within an AI regulatory sandbox under Article 58, the market surveillance authorities shall verify the compliance with Article 60 as part of their supervisory role for the AI regulatory sandbox. Those authorities may, as appropriate, allow the testing in real world conditions to be conducted by the provider or prospective provider, in derogation from the conditions set out in Article 60(4), points (f) and (g).
@ref Art 76(2) second sentence (src:1265)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the testing in real world conditions is conducted for AI systems that are supervised within an AI regulatory sandbox under Article 58` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 76(2) second sentence the market surveillance authorities may allow the testing to be conducted by the provider or prospective provider in derogation from the conditions set out in Article 60(4), points (f) and (g)` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the group General applies from the date Art 113 gives
    ELSE IF NOT `the testing in real world conditions is conducted for AI systems that are supervised within an AI regulatory sandbox under Article 58`
         THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Those authorities", the authorities of the "Where" case of the first sentence (a "may" gated by "where": split site (ii), fork F-76-2-where)
         ELSE IF `it is appropriate`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "as appropriate" limits the power; the grant ruling of 2026-11-12 gives NOTHING for a failed gate of a power (fork F-76-2-appropriate)

-- src:1265 | 2. Where testing in real world conditions is conducted for AI systems that are supervised within an AI regulatory sandbox under Article 58, the market surveillance authorities shall verify the compliance with Article 60 as part of their supervisory role for the AI regulatory sandbox. Those authorities may, as appropriate, allow the testing in real world conditions to be conducted by the provider or prospective provider, in derogation from the conditions set out in Article 60(4), points (f) and (g).
@ref Art 76(2) second sentence (src:1265)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the testing in real world conditions is conducted for AI systems that are supervised within an AI regulatory sandbox under Article 58` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Arts 72 to 79 party` `Art 76 act`
`Art 76(2) second sentence the market surveillance authority's choice to allow the testing in derogation` MEANS
    IF (NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)) OR (NOT `the testing in real world conditions is conducted for AI systems that are supervised within an AI regulatory sandbox under Article 58`) OR (NOT `it is appropriate`)
    THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the group General does not apply on the date asked, or the conditions of the duty are not met
    ELSE
        PARTY `Arts 72 to 79 party market surveillance authority`
        MAY `Art 76(2) allow the testing in real world conditions to be conducted by the provider or prospective provider in derogation from the conditions set out in Article 60(4), points (f) and (g)`
        HENCE FULFILLED

§ `Article 76(3) to (5): decisions`

-- src:1266 | 3. Where a market surveillance authority has been informed by the prospective provider, the provider or any third party of a serious incident or has other grounds for considering that the conditions set out in Articles 60 and 61 are not met, it may take either of the following decisions on its territory, as appropriate:
-- src:1267 | (a) to suspend or terminate the testing in real world conditions;
-- src:1268 | (b) to require the provider or prospective provider and the deployer or prospective deployer to modify any aspect of the testing in real world conditions.
@ref Art 76(3) and points (a), (b) (src:1266-1268)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the market surveillance authority has been informed by the prospective provider, the provider or any third party of a serious incident` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the market surveillance authority has other grounds for considering that the conditions set out in Articles 60 and 61 are not met` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 76(3) the market surveillance authority may take the decision on its territory` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the group General applies from the date Art 113 gives
    ELSE IF (NOT `the market surveillance authority has been informed by the prospective provider, the provider or any third party of a serious incident`) AND (NOT `the market surveillance authority has other grounds for considering that the conditions set out in Articles 60 and 61 are not met`)
         THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a market surveillance authority has been informed ... of a serious incident or has other grounds ..., it may take either of the following decisions on its territory" (a "may" gated by "where": split site (ii), fork F-76-3-where)
         ELSE IF `it is appropriate`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "as appropriate" limits the power (fork F-76-3-appropriate)

-- src:1266 | 3. Where a market surveillance authority has been informed by the prospective provider, the provider or any third party of a serious incident or has other grounds for considering that the conditions set out in Articles 60 and 61 are not met, it may take either of the following decisions on its territory, as appropriate:
-- src:1267 | (a) to suspend or terminate the testing in real world conditions;
@ref Art 76(3) point (a) (src:1266-1267)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the market surveillance authority has been informed by the prospective provider, the provider or any third party of a serious incident` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the market surveillance authority has other grounds for considering that the conditions set out in Articles 60 and 61 are not met` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Arts 72 to 79 party` `Art 76 act`
`Art 76(3) point (a) the market surveillance authority's choice to suspend or terminate the testing` MEANS
    IF     (NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`))
        OR ((NOT `the market surveillance authority has been informed by the prospective provider, the provider or any third party of a serious incident`) AND (NOT `the market surveillance authority has other grounds for considering that the conditions set out in Articles 60 and 61 are not met`))
        OR (NOT `it is appropriate`)
    THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is permitted: the group General does not apply on the date asked, no ground of the "where" clause holds, or it is not appropriate
    ELSE
        PARTY `Arts 72 to 79 party market surveillance authority`
        MAY `Art 76(3)(a) suspend or terminate the testing in real world conditions`
        HENCE FULFILLED

-- src:1266 | 3. Where a market surveillance authority has been informed by the prospective provider, the provider or any third party of a serious incident or has other grounds for considering that the conditions set out in Articles 60 and 61 are not met, it may take either of the following decisions on its territory, as appropriate:
-- src:1267 | (a) to suspend or terminate the testing in real world conditions;
-- src:1268 | (b) to require the provider or prospective provider and the deployer or prospective deployer to modify any aspect of the testing in real world conditions.
@ref Art 76(3) point (b) (src:1266-1268)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the market surveillance authority has been informed by the prospective provider, the provider or any third party of a serious incident` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the market surveillance authority has other grounds for considering that the conditions set out in Articles 60 and 61 are not met` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Arts 72 to 79 party` `Art 76 act`
`Art 76(3) point (b) the market surveillance authority's choice to require the modification of the testing` MEANS
    IF     (NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`))
        OR ((NOT `the market surveillance authority has been informed by the prospective provider, the provider or any third party of a serious incident`) AND (NOT `the market surveillance authority has other grounds for considering that the conditions set out in Articles 60 and 61 are not met`))
        OR (NOT `it is appropriate`)
    THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is permitted: the group General does not apply on the date asked, no ground of the "where" clause holds, or it is not appropriate
    ELSE
        PARTY `Arts 72 to 79 party market surveillance authority`
        MAY `Art 76(3)(b) require the provider or prospective provider and the deployer or prospective deployer to modify any aspect of the testing in real world conditions`
        HENCE FULFILLED

-- src:1269 | 4. Where a market surveillance authority has taken a decision referred to in paragraph 3 of this Article, or has issued an objection within the meaning of Article 60(4), point (b), the decision or the objection shall indicate the grounds therefor and how the provider or prospective provider can challenge the decision or objection.
@ref Art 76(4) (src:1269)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the market surveillance authority has taken a decision referred to in paragraph 3, or has issued an objection within the meaning of Article 60(4), point (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision or the objection indicates the grounds` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision or the objection indicates how the provider or prospective provider can challenge it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 76(4) the decision or the objection indicates the grounds and how the provider or prospective provider can challenge it` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the group General applies from the date Art 113 gives
    ELSE IF `the market surveillance authority has taken a decision referred to in paragraph 3, or has issued an objection within the meaning of Article 60(4), point (b)` AND `the decision or the objection indicates the grounds` AND `the decision or the objection indicates how the provider or prospective provider can challenge it`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a market surveillance authority has taken a decision ..., the decision or the objection shall indicate the grounds therefor and how the provider or prospective provider can challenge" (a bare "shall" not done, taken case by case)

-- src:1269 | 4. Where a market surveillance authority has taken a decision referred to in paragraph 3 of this Article, or has issued an objection within the meaning of Article 60(4), point (b), the decision or the objection shall indicate the grounds therefor and how the provider or prospective provider can challenge the decision or objection.
@ref Art 76(4) (src:1269)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the market surveillance authority has taken a decision referred to in paragraph 3, or has issued an objection within the meaning of Article 60(4), point (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Arts 72 to 79 party` `Art 76 act`
`Art 76(4) the market surveillance authority's duty to indicate the grounds and how the decision or objection can be challenged` MEANS
    IF (NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)) OR (NOT `the market surveillance authority has taken a decision referred to in paragraph 3, or has issued an objection within the meaning of Article 60(4), point (b)`)
    THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the group General does not apply on the date asked, or the conditions of the duty are not met
    ELSE
        PARTY `Arts 72 to 79 party market surveillance authority`
        MUST `Art 76(4) indicate the grounds of the decision or objection and how the provider or prospective provider can challenge it`
        HENCE FULFILLED

-- src:1270 | 5. Where applicable, where a market surveillance authority has taken a decision referred to in paragraph 3, it shall communicate the grounds therefor to the market surveillance authorities of other Member States in which the AI system has been tested in accordance with the testing plan.
@ref Art 76(5) (src:1270)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the communication is applicable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the market surveillance authority has taken a decision referred to in paragraph 3` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the AI system has been tested in accordance with the testing plan in other Member States` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 76(5) the market surveillance authority must communicate the grounds to the market surveillance authorities of other Member States in which the AI system has been tested` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the group General applies from the date Art 113 gives
    ELSE IF `the communication is applicable` AND `the market surveillance authority has taken a decision referred to in paragraph 3` AND `the AI system has been tested in accordance with the testing plan in other Member States`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where applicable, where a market surveillance authority has taken a decision referred to in paragraph 3, it shall communicate the grounds therefor" (an unmet "where" gate counts as the text's no: ruling (b)) (fork F-76-5-duty)

-- src:1270 | 5. Where applicable, where a market surveillance authority has taken a decision referred to in paragraph 3, it shall communicate the grounds therefor to the market surveillance authorities of other Member States in which the AI system has been tested in accordance with the testing plan.
@ref Art 76(5) (src:1270)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the communication is applicable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the market surveillance authority has taken a decision referred to in paragraph 3` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the AI system has been tested in accordance with the testing plan in other Member States` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Arts 72 to 79 party` `Art 76 act`
`Art 76(5) the market surveillance authority's duty to communicate the grounds to the market surveillance authorities of other Member States` MEANS
    IF (NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)) OR (NOT `the communication is applicable`) OR (NOT `the market surveillance authority has taken a decision referred to in paragraph 3`) OR (NOT `the AI system has been tested in accordance with the testing plan in other Member States`)
    THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the group General does not apply on the date asked, or the conditions of the duty are not met
    ELSE
        PARTY `Arts 72 to 79 party market surveillance authority`
        MUST `Art 76(5) communicate the grounds of the decision to the market surveillance authorities of other Member States in which the AI system has been tested in accordance with the testing plan`
        HENCE FULFILLED
